          <p class="auth-msg" id="kp-msg" role="status"></p>
          <div class="keeper-out" id="kp-out" hidden></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="muted xsmall">Every clip is <strong>generated, not filmed</strong>: nothing here records a
      real event, and it should never be presented as though it did. Video needs a GPU somewhere even when
      the model is open — if no video key is connected to this project, ShakDrah will say so rather than
      pretend.</p>
    </div>

<div class="draw-box model-box reveal" id="model-box">
      <p class="kicker">THE TURNING SHOP</p>
      <h3>Make a 3D Model</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Build a thing out of solids. Add a box, a sphere, a cylinder, a cone or a
      torus; move it, turn it, scale it, colour it, and the piece assembles in the window below. It is
      deliberately simple &mdash; blocks and primitives, the way a model is roughed out before it is
      sculpted. Nothing is sent anywhere: the whole shop runs in this page. When you are done, take the
      model away as an <strong>OBJ</strong> file any 3D program will open, or hand the view to ShakDrah and
      let him render it as a photograph.</p>

      <div class="model-stage" id="model-stage" role="img"
           aria-label="A three-dimensional workspace showing the model being built"></div>

      <div class="write-model" id="md-write-box">
        <p class="kicker">BUILD IT FROM WORDS</p>
        <form class="ornate" id="md-write-form">
          <label for="md-write">Describe a model</label>
          <textarea id="md-write" rows="2" maxlength="600" required
            placeholder="A small stone chapel with a slate roof, an arched door and a bell tower at the west end"></textarea>
          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn btn--small" type="submit" id="md-write-go">Build it</button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <p class="auth-msg" id="md-write-msg"></p>
        <p class="muted xsmall">A model is asked for a <em>plan</em> rather than a mesh &mdash; which
        pieces, at what size, turned which way, standing where &mdash; and the shop builds that plan out
        of the same solids and the same pattern book you would have dragged into place yourself. So what
        arrives has named parts, can be unstitched and worked on, and exports as an OBJ like everything
        else. It is a rough carpenter, not a sculptor: expect to move things.</p>
      </div>

      <details class="scroll scan" id="scan-box">
        <summary>Scan something real with the camera</summary>
        <p class="muted small">Two photographs make a solid. The outline of the first gives the width of
        every slice of the thing; the outline of the second, taken a quarter turn round, gives the depth of
        the same slice. Sweep those two profiles together and you have a shape with the photograph wrapped
        over the front of it. One photograph still works &mdash; the depth is then guessed from the width,
        which is right for a mug and wrong for a book, and the page will say so. <strong>Nothing leaves
        this page:</strong> the camera stream, the frames and the finished mesh are all made and kept in
        your own browser.</p>

        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="What to scan">
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-scan-mode="object" aria-pressed="true">An object</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-scan-mode="face" aria-pressed="false">Your face</button>
        </div>

        <div class="scan-grid">
          <div>
            <video id="scan-video" class="scan-video" playsinline muted hidden></video>
            <div class="sketch-group">
              <button class="btn btn--small" type="button" id="scan-start">Turn the camera on</button>
              <button class="btn btn--small btn--ghost" type="button" id="scan-stop" hidden>Camera off</button>
              <button class="btn btn--small" type="button" id="scan-capture" hidden>Take the photograph</button>
              <button class="btn btn--small btn--ghost" type="button" id="scan-skip" hidden>Skip this one</button>
            </div>
            <p class="muted xsmall">No camera, or a better photograph already taken?
              <input type="file" id="scan-file" accept="image/*" class="sound-file"></p>
            <div class="scan-shots" id="scan-shots"></div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <ol class="scan-steps" id="scan-steps"></ol>
            <canvas id="scan-preview" class="scan-preview" width="300" height="300" hidden
                    role="img" aria-label="The cut-out made from your photographs"></canvas>
            <p class="auth-msg" id="scan-status"></p>
            <div class="sketch-group" id="scan-done" hidden>
              <button class="btn btn--small" type="button" id="scan-to-bench">Put it on the bench</button>
              <button class="btn btn--small" type="button" id="scan-to-pad">Send it to the sketch pad</button>
              <button class="btn btn--small btn--ghost" type="button" id="scan-redo">Start again</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <div class="model-tools">
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Add a solid">
          <button class="tool" type="button" id="md-book"
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pattern-book">Objects</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="box">Box</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="sphere">Sphere</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="cylinder">Cylinder</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="cone">Cone</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="torus">Torus</button>
        </div>
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Colour">
          <button class="swatch is-on" type="button" data-colour="#d7b05a" aria-label="Gold"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#b8c0cc" aria-label="Steel"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#8a5a33" aria-label="Wood"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#5f9e58" aria-label="Green"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#2f6fa8" aria-label="Blue"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#c8352f" aria-label="Red"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#1b1b1f" aria-label="Near black"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#efe3c8" aria-label="Bone"></button>
          <span class="colour-any">
            <label for="md-rgb">Any colour</label>
            <input id="md-rgb" type="color" value="#d7b05a">
            <input id="md-hex" type="text" maxlength="7" spellcheck="false"
                   autocomplete="off" aria-label="Colour as a hex code" value="#d7b05a">
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Surface">
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-finish="matt">Matt</button>
          <button class="tool is-on" type="button" data-finish="satin">Satin</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-finish="metal">Metal</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-finish="glass">Glass</button>
        </div>
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="History">
